# Simonethg test UI + README — mandatory for every deliverable

## Rule

Every feature, library, or onchain helper we ship in this repo **must** include:

1. A simple manual test UI under `packages/nextjs`, branded as Simonethg.
2. An updated README (root and any package README) that stays honest about what exists today.
3. Screenshots in `docs/screenshots/` when there is a UI, referenced from the README.
4. Footer/credit line: **Powered by [AcademiaQA.com](https://academiaqa.com)** in every README.

No “library-only” days without a playground page (or an extension of an existing playground section).

## Brand tokens (simonethg.com)

Use CSS variables — do not invent a purple/indigo or terracotta theme:

| Token | Value | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `--sg-bg` | `#F4F2EA` | Page background |
| `--sg-ink` | `#0A0A0A` | Body text, headings |
| `--sg-accent` | `#FFBC00` | Primary CTA, focus ring, highlights |
| `--sg-accent-hover` | `#E6AD00` | Hover on primary |
| `--sg-muted` | `#5A5E7A` | Secondary text (must still pass AA on `--sg-bg`) |
| `--sg-surface` | `#FFFFFF` | Interactive panels only when needed |
| Font display | **Baloo 2** | Brand mark, H1 |
| Font body | **DM Sans** | UI copy, forms (readable; not Inter/Roboto/Arial/system) |

Brand mark in the chrome: **Simonethg** linking to `https://simonethg.com`. Product name secondary: **scaffold-arc**.

## UX / UI practices

- One job per screen/section: one headline, one short supporting line, one primary action group.
- Prefer open layout over card walls. Cards only when they contain an interaction (form, calculator, result).
- Visible focus (`:focus-visible`) using `--sg-accent`. Touch targets ≥ 44×44 px (WCAG 2.5.5).
- Primary selectors: `data-testid`. Aria roles secondary. Never rely on CSS class selectors for tests.
- Playground UI is **multilingual** — see `.cursor/rules/simonethg-i18n.mdc`: locales `en`, `es`, `pt-BR`, `zh`, `ar` (RTL). Flag-only switcher with `aria-label`s. Do not hardcode UI copy in one language.
- Show fees and balances in **USD / USDC**, never raw Gwei as the only unit.
- Single USDC balance in any wallet UI — never native + ERC-20 as two rows.
- Header logo: **mascot image** only (`data-testid="brand-mascot"`), linking to simonethg.com — no personal name wordmark. Product name secondary: **scaffold-arc**.

## ADA (every UI change)

- axe-core scan **scoped to the changed component**, viewports **390 px** and **1440 px**.
- Critical / serious → block merge. Moderate / minor → document as observations.
- Applicable: 1.4.3 contrast, 2.1.1 keyboard, 2.4.7 focus visible, 4.1.2 name/role/value, 2.5.5 target size, 2.5.3 label in name.
- Code comments in English; user-facing playground strings via i18n dictionaries (not a single hard-coded language).

## README format (every README)

Always two sections, in this order:

### Para todos (first)

- What it is in plain language (Spanish or English matching the audience; root README can be English for global builders, with a short Spanish blurb if useful).
- Screenshots of the UI under `docs/screenshots/` referenced in markdown.
- Important functions explained without jargon.

### Para developers (second)

- Clone / yarn / forge test / yarn nextjs:dev — the fast path.
- Keep the README updated with what actually exists today (checkboxes that match reality).

### In ALL READMEs

```markdown
**Powered by [AcademiaQA.com](https://academiaqa.com)**
```

## Where UI lives

- App: `packages/nextjs`
- Shared brand CSS: `packages/nextjs/app/globals.css`
- Each major feature gets a route or a clearly labeled section, e.g. `/playground/usdc`, `/playground/memo`
- Screenshots: `docs/screenshots/`
